{"error":false,"activeTest":false,"task":{"id":14252060,"type":"Review","status":"Processed","importance":1,"reason":null,"locked":null,"proofId":null,"currentQuestionId":null,"currentQuestionTimestamp":null,"progress":1,"points":4,"passed":1,"rawPointsAwarded":4,"pointsAwarded":4,"mp":null,"mpAwarded":null,"mpDecayRate":null,"student":{"id":57975,"firstName":"Harrison","lastName":"Charles","locale":null,"subscriptionId":"sub_1UO3yHD4gcTFRx97dYjQXmX1","sequenceId":19},"course":{"id":111,"name":"Mathematical Foundations II"},"topic":{"id":2883,"name":"Dividing Polynomials by Manipulating Rational Expressions"},"test":{"id":null,"name":null,"diagnostic":null,"timeLimit":null,"questionCount":null},"created":"2026-10-16T00:01:34.000Z","started":"2026-10-16T00:12:19.000Z","completed":"2026-10-16T00:14:23.000Z","processed":"2026-10-16T00:14:44.000Z","progressStr":"100%","answers":[{"id":62310648,"created":"2026-10-16T00:12:51.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":32217,"number":1,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 12:12 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:32","question":{"id":87780,"format":"MC","difficulty":3,"exampleId":7722,"text":"<p>Write $\\dfrac{12x^3}{4x^2+5}$ in the form $ax + \\dfrac{bx}{4x^2+5},$ where $a \\neq 0.$ What is the value of $a+b?$</p>\n","choice1":" $-12$","choice2":" $-9$","choice3":" $-6$","choice4":" $-3$","choice5":" $0$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>First, we factor the numerator to put $4x^2$ in parentheses. Then, we add and subtract $5$ in the parentheses. This reveals a copy of the denominator without changing the value of the expression.</p>\n<p>\\[\\begin{align*}\n\\dfrac{12x^3}{4x^2+5} &= \\dfrac{3x(4x^2)}{4x^2+5} \\\\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac{3x(4x^2+5-5)}{4x^2+5} \\\\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac{3x(4x^2+5) + 3x(-5)}{4x^2+5} \\\\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac{3x(4x^2+5)-15x}{4x^2+5} \n\\end{align*}\\]</p>\n<p>Then, we split the fraction into two, and then simplify:</p>\n<p>\\[\\begin{align*}\n\\dfrac{3x(4x^2+5)-15x}{4x^2+5}  &= \\dfrac{3x(4x^2+5)}{4x^2+5}  + \\dfrac{-15x}{4x^2+5}  \\\\[5pt]\n&= 3x + \\dfrac{-15x}{4x^2+5} \\\\[5pt]\n\\end{align*}\\]</p>\n<p>Therefore, we have $a=3$ and $b=-15,$ and we get\n\\[\na + b = 3 + (-15) = -12.\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2883,"name":"Dividing Polynomials by Manipulating Rational Expressions"},"example":{"id":7722,"title":"Manipulating Rational Expressions With Single-Term Numerators When Factoring Is Required"},"group":{"id":158755,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[{"id":null,"number":null,"answers":[]}],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14252060,"answer":{"id":62310648,"cread":"2026-10-16T00:12:51.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":32217},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyHard","difficultySymbol":"H","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62310660,"created":"2026-10-16T00:13:08.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13649,"number":2,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 12:13 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:14","question":{"id":88260,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":7721,"text":"<p>Write $\\dfrac{4x-1}{4x-7}$ in the form $a + \\dfrac{b}{4x-7},$ where $a \\neq 0.$ What is the value of $a+b?$</p>\n","choice1":"$7$","choice2":"$5$","choice3":"$-5$","choice4":"$4$","choice5":"$6$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>First, we subtract and add $7$ in the numerator. This reveals a copy of the denominator without changing the value of the expression.</p>\n<p>\\[\\begin{align*}\n\\dfrac{4x-1}{4x-7} = \\dfrac{4x-7+7-1}{4x-7}\n\\end{align*}\\]</p>\n<p>Then, we split the fraction into two, and then simplify:</p>\n<p>\\[\\begin{align*}\n\\dfrac{4x-7+7-1}{4x-7} &= \\dfrac{4x-7}{4x-7} + \\dfrac{7-1}{4x-7} \\\\[5pt]\n&= 1 + \\dfrac{6}{4x-7} \\\\[5pt]\n\\end{align*}\\]</p>\n<p>Therefore, we have $a=1$ and $b=6,$ and we get</p>\n<p>\\[\na + b = 1 + 6 = 7.\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2883,"name":"Dividing Polynomials by Manipulating Rational Expressions"},"example":{"id":7721,"title":"Manipulating Rational Expressions With Two-Term Numerators"},"group":{"id":157310,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14252060,"answer":{"id":62310660,"cread":"2026-10-16T00:13:08.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13649},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62310675,"created":"2026-10-16T00:13:29.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":null,"freeResponse":"[\"2\",\"x+11\"]","timeElapsed":16596,"number":3,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 12:13 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:17","question":{"id":319887,"format":"FR","difficulty":2,"exampleId":7721,"text":"Write $\\dfrac{7x^2+11}{7x^2-x}$ in the form $a + \\dfrac{bx+c}{7x^2-x},$ where $a \\neq 0.$","choice1":null,"choice2":null,"choice3":null,"choice4":null,"choice5":null,"freeAnswerChoice":"<table rules=all cellpadding=1 align=\"center\" style=\"border:1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 4mm; margin-top: 4mm\">\n<tr>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"25\" style=\"text-align:center; border:1px solid black; border-left:hidden; border-top:hidden;\">$7x^2+11$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" rowspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center; border:hidden;\">$\\large =$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" rowspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center; border:hidden;\">\n[\n    answer: 1;\n    type: number;\n    width: 30;\n    margin-left: 6;\n    margin-right: 1;\n]\n</td>\n<td width=\"20\" rowspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center; border:hidden;\">$+$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"25\" style=\"text-align:center; border:1px solid black; border-right:hidden; border-top:hidden;\">\n[\n    answer: x+11;\n    type: expression;\n    width: 70;\n    margin-left: 1;\n    margin-right: 1;\n    buttons: exp;\n] \n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"25\" style=\"text-align:center; border-left:hidden; border-bottom:hidden;\">$7x^2-x$</td>\n<td width=\"25\" height=\"25\" style=\"text-align:center; border-right:hidden; border-bottom:hidden;\">$7x^2-x$</td>\n</tr>\n</table>","explanation":"<p>First, we add and subtract $x$ in the numerator. This reveals a copy of the denominator without changing the value of the expression.</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n\\dfrac{7x^2+11}{7x^2-x} \\;=\\; \\dfrac{7x^2-x+x+11}{7x^2-x}\n\\end{align*}\n\\]</p>\n<p>Then, we split the fraction into two, and then simplify:</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n\\dfrac{7x^2-x+x+11}{7x^2-x}\n&= \\dfrac{7x^2-x}{7x^2-x} + \\dfrac{x+11}{7x^2-x} \\\\[5pt]\n&= \\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid gainsboro]{1} + \\dfrac{\\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid gainsboro]{x+11}}{7x^2-x}\n\\end{align*}\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2883,"name":"Dividing Polynomials by Manipulating Rational Expressions"},"example":{"id":7721,"title":"Manipulating Rational Expressions With Two-Term Numerators"},"group":{"id":157649,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14252060,"answer":{"id":62310675,"cread":"2026-10-16T00:13:29.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":null,"freeResponse":["2","x+11"],"timeElapsed":16596},"graphic":false,"freeResponse":{"segments":[{"text":"<table rules=all cellpadding=1 align=\"center\" style=\"border:1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 4mm; margin-top: 4mm\">\n<tr>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"25\" style=\"text-align:center; border:1px solid black; border-left:hidden; border-top:hidden;\">$7x^2+11$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" rowspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center; border:hidden;\">$\\large =$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" rowspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center; border:hidden;\">\n"},{"textbox":{"answer":"1","type":"number","width":30,"margin":{"left":6,"right":1},"buttons":[]}},{"text":"\n</td>\n<td width=\"20\" rowspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center; border:hidden;\">$+$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"25\" style=\"text-align:center; border:1px solid black; border-right:hid