dth=\"20\" height=\"25\" style=\"text-align:center; border-left:hidden; border-bottom:hidden;\">$3x^6+2x$</td>\n<td width=\"25\" height=\"25\" style=\"text-align:center; border-right:hidden; border-bottom:hidden;\">$3x^6+2x$</td>\n</tr>\n</table>","explanation":"<p>First, we add and subtract $2x$ in the numerator. This reveals a copy of the denominator without changing the value of the expression.</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n\\dfrac{3x^6+8}{3x^6+2x} \\;=\\; \\dfrac{3x^6+2x-2x+8}{3x^6+2x}\n\\end{align*}\n\\]</p>\n<p>Then, we split the fraction into two, and then simplify:</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n\\dfrac{3x^6+2x-2x+8}{3x^6+2x}\n&= \\dfrac{3x^6+2x}{3x^4+2x} + \\dfrac{-2x+8}{3x^6+2x} \\\\[5pt]\n&= 1 + \\dfrac{-2x+8}{3x^6+2x}\n\\end{align*}\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2883,"name":"Dividing Polynomials by Manipulating Rational Expressions"},"example":{"id":7721,"title":"Manipulating Rational Expressions With Two-Term Numerators"},"group":{"id":158156,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14252060,"answer":{"id":62310683,"cread":"2026-10-16T00:13:52.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":null,"freeResponse":["1","-2x+8"],"timeElapsed":18696},"graphic":false,"freeResponse":{"segments":[{"text":"<table rules=all cellpadding=1 align=\"center\" style=\"border:1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 4mm; margin-top: 4mm\">\n<tr>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"25\" style=\"text-align:center; border:1px solid black; border-left:hidden; border-top:hidden;\">$3x^6+8$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" rowspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center; border:hidden;\">$\\large =$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" rowspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center; border:hidden;\">\n"},{"textbox":{"answer":"1","type":"number","width":35,"margin":{"left":6,"right":1},"buttons":[]}},{"text":"\n</td>\n<td width=\"20\" rowspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center; border:hidden;\">$+$</td>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"25\" style=\"text-align:center; border:1px solid black; border-right:hidden; border-top:hidden;\">\n"},{"textbox":{"answer":"-2x+8","type":"expression","width":70,"margin":{"left":1,"right":1},"buttons":["exp"]}},{"text":" \n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"20\" height=\"25\" style=\"text-align:center; border-left:hidden; border-bottom:hidden;\">$3x^6+2x$</td>\n<td width=\"25\" height=\"25\" style=\"text-align:center; border-right:hidden; border-bottom:hidden;\">$3x^6+2x$</td>\n</tr>\n</table>"}]},"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62310699,"created":"2026-10-16T00:14:22.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":null,"freeResponse":"[\"2\",\"-8\"]","timeElapsed":25534,"number":5,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 12:14 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:26","question":{"id":320766,"format":"FR","difficulty":3,"exampleId":7722,"text":"Write $\\dfrac{12x^7}{6x^7+4}$ in the form $a + \\dfrac{b}{6x^7+4},$ where $a \\neq 0.$","choice1":null,"choice2":null,"choice3":null,"choice4":null,"choice5":null,"freeAnswerChoice":"<table rules=all cellpadding=1 align=\"center\" style=\"border:1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 4mm; margin-top: 4mm\">\n<tr>\n<td width=\"30\" height=\"25\" style=\"text-align:center; border:1px solid black; border-left:hidden; border-top:hidden;\">$12x^7$</td>\n<td width=\"25\" rowspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center; border:hidden;\">$\\large =$</td>\n<td width=\"30\" rowspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center; border:hidden;\">\n[\n    answer: 2;\n    type: number;\n    width: 35;\n    margin-left: 4;\n    margin-right: 1;\n]\n</td>\n<td width=\"25\" rowspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center; border:hidden;\">$+$</td>\n<td width=\"60\" height=\"25\" style=\"text-align:center; border:1px solid black; border-right:hidden; border-top:hidden;\">\n[\n    answer: -8;\n    type: number;\n    width: 40;\n    margin-left: 0;\n    margin-right: 0;\n]\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"30\" height=\"25\" style=\"text-align:center; border-left:hidden; border-bottom:hidden;\">$6x^7+4$</td>\n<td width=\"60\" height=\"25\" style=\"text-align:center; border-right:hidden; border-bottom:hidden;\">$6x^7+4$</td>\n</tr>\n</table>","explanation":"<p>First, we factor the numerator to put $6x^7$ in parentheses. Then, we add and subtract $4$ in the parentheses. This reveals a copy of the denominator without changing the value of the expression.</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n\\dfrac{12x^7}{6x^7+4}\n&= \\dfrac{2(6x^7)}{6x^7+4} \\\\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac{2(6x^7+4-4)}{6x^7+4} \\\\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac{2[(6x^7+4)-(4)]}{6x^7+4} \\\\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac{2(6x^7+4)-2(4)}{6x^7+4} \\\\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac{2(6x^7+4)-8}{6x^7+4}\n\\end{align*}\n\\]</p>\n<p>Then, we split the fraction into two, and then simplify:</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n\\dfrac{2(6x^7+4)-8}{6x^7+4}\n&= \\dfrac{2(6x^7+4)}{6x^7+4} + \\dfrac{-8}{6x^7+4} \\\\[5pt]\n&= \\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid gainsboro]{2} + \\dfrac{\\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid gainsboro]{-8}}{6x^7+4}\n\\end{align*}\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2883,"name":"Dividing Polynomials by Manipulating Rational Expressions"},"example":{"id":7722,"title":"Manipulating Rational Expressions With Single-Term Numerators When Factoring Is Required"},"group":{"id":158863,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14252060,"answer":{"id":62310699,"cread":"2026-10-16T00:14:22.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":null,"freeResponse":["2","-8"],"timeElapsed":25534},"graphic":false,"freeResponse":{"segments":[{"text":"<table rules=all cellpadding=1 align=\"center\" style=\"border:1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 4mm; margin-top: 4mm\">\n<tr>\n<td width=\"30\" height=\"25\" style=\"text-align:center; border:1px solid black; border-left:hidden; border-top:hidden;\">$12x^7$</td>\n<td width=\"25\" rowspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center; border:hidden;\">$\\large =$</td>\n<td width=\"30\" rowspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center; border:hidden;\">\n"},{"textbox":{"answer":"2